"""
t0_taxonomy.py -- hand-authored Requirement Type / Category / Subcategory
classification and genuinely tailored (non-generic) deliverable + evidence
text for the 43 T0 Gate RTMs, per GBO's request for real per-row nuance
rather than templated boilerplate.

Classification rule (recorded in full on the TAXONOMY sheet):
  SYSTEM  -- a technical property/behaviour the QPS itself must exhibit,
             verified by calc/test/design review. Sub: Performance /
             Constraint / Control.
  PROJECT -- an action or administrative responsibility the Contractor (the
             organisation) must carry out -- a WBS task, not a system
             property. Sub: Documentation & Compliance / Governance &
             Responsibility / Quality Assurance.
  SAFETY  -- the requirement's SUBJECT is hazard elimination/mitigation to
             personnel or equipment. Sub: Personnel Protection / Equipment
             Protection / Interlock & Control Safety / Regulatory-Certification.
  Many T0 items are dual-natured (e.g. "submit a risk analysis" is a PROJECT
  action about a SAFETY subject) -- SAFETY is used when the hazard itself is
  the requirement's substance; PROJECT is used when the ask is fundamentally
  administrative even if safety-adjacent. This is a judgment call, flagged
  here rather than hidden.

Each entry: (type, category, subcategory, deliverable_override_or_None,
             evidence_text). deliverable_override is None when the existing
             M-column text is already specific enough to keep as-is.
"""

